0..77 Comment "// A program decides a compact bounded universal through `std.reals.Eff`, the"
78..161 Comment "// host interface of exact reals. The universal is `∀ x ∈ [0, 1] (x · x < 2)`."
162..237 Comment "// `gandr run forall.gandr` prints `holds`. The same `decided` runs under a"
238..297 Comment "// handler of this source, a second model of the interface."
298..300 Comment "//"
301..377 Comment "// The domain of the plan is the closed interval `[0, 1]`. The domain states"
378..453 Comment "// its overtness at the reference 1 and its compactness at the reference 2."
454..530 Comment "// The universal names the compactness as its evidence, and the overtness as"
531..595 Comment "// the evidence of its dual. The host registers both references."
596..598 Comment "//"
599..676 Comment "// `decide` mints a machine on the two poles of the root. The pole that holds"
677..753 Comment "// covers the domain with subintervals where the body holds. It certifies in"
754..829 Comment "// 5 steps, and the checker replays its certificate before the host replies"
830..907 Comment "// `holds`. The pole that fails suspends after 3 steps, so the machine spends"
908..940 Comment "// 8 quanta of its budget of 16."
941..943 Comment "//"
944..1013 Comment "// - see: `corpus/model/reals/exists.gandr` — the overt existential"
1014..1088 Comment "// - see: `crates/theory-exact-reals/src/bisection.rs` — the search of a"
1089..1104 Comment "//   quantifier"
1106..1138 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
